WEBVTT

1
00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:02.261
Episode five: working offline.

2
00:00:02.612 --> 00:00:07.876
Technicians often work in basements with no signal, so the form keeps working offline.

3
00:00:07.876 --> 00:00:12.100
Three browser features make that possible: IndexedDB stores the data,

4
00:00:12.100 --> 00:00:17.670
localStorage is a simple fallback for drafts, and a service worker stores the page’s files.

5
00:00:18.022 --> 00:00:21.891
Save draft keeps every answer, and in offline mode the photos too.

6
00:00:22.243 --> 00:00:26.801
Reload the page, and the answers come back, with a banner to discard the draft.

7
00:00:27.628 --> 00:00:30.177
If a report is submitted with no connection,

8
00:00:30.177 --> 00:00:34.637
it goes into an outbox in IndexedDB, and the form says one report is waiting.

9
00:00:34.989 --> 00:00:40.453
When the connection comes back, OfflineSync sends the waiting reports, oldest first.

10
00:00:40.453 --> 00:00:43.315
A temporary failure is simply retried later.

11
00:00:43.315 --> 00:00:47.739
A report the CRM refuses is kept, marked as failed, and not retried.

12
00:00:48.090 --> 00:00:50.922
The page itself opens without a network, too.

13
00:00:50.922 --> 00:00:55.957
On the first visit, the service worker keeps a copy of every file the page used.

14
00:00:55.957 --> 00:00:59.608
Later, if the network fails, it answers from those copies.

15
00:00:59.959 --> 00:01:02.078
You have now seen the whole codebase.

16
00:01:02.078 --> 00:01:05.687
When something looks wrong, start with these debugging recipes.

17
00:01:06.038 --> 00:01:10.122
And to really learn it, do the first tasks at the end of the code guide.

18
00:01:10.122 --> 00:01:14.148
Each one is a small, real change, with the answer hidden until you try.

19
00:01:14.498 --> 00:01:16.041
That is the end of the tour.

20
00:01:16.041 --> 00:01:18.246
Thanks for watching, and happy building.
